ns of $f$ and a restricted Gaussian oracle (RGO) for $g$. The latter requirement means that we can easily sample from the density $\\text{RGO}_{g,h,y}(x) \\propto \\exp(-g(x) -\\frac{1}{2h}||y-x||^2)$, which is the sampling analogue of the proximal operator for $g$. If $f + g$ is $α$-strongly convex and $f$ is $β$-smooth, our sampler achieves $\\varepsilon$ error in total variation distance in $\\widetilde{\\mathcal O}(κ\\sqrt d \\log^4(1/\\varepsilon))$ iterations where $κ:= β/α$, which matches prior state-of-the-art results for the case $g=0$. We further extend our results to cases where (1) $π$ is non-log-concave but satisfies a Poincaré or log-Sobolev inequality, and (2) $f$ is non-smooth but Lipschitz.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSearch Results - \"Error analysis in mathematics\" :: Library Catalog (https://iris.sena.edu.co/EDS/Search?dfApplied=1&filter%5B%5D=EXPAND%3A%22fulltext%22&filter%5B%5D=SubjectEDS%3A%22distribution+%28probability+theory%29%22&lookfor=%22Error+analysis+in+mathematics%22&type=SU)\nciteturn4search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Aug2026, Vol. ... ## Shifted Composition III: Local Error Framework for KL Divergence.Authors: Altschuler, Jason M.Chewi, Sinho\n\nAcademic Journal\n\n## Error Estimation for Approximate Solutions to the Minimum Entropy Coupling Problem.\n\nAuthors: HAO, Yifei WANG, Yingzhe\n\nSource: Chinese Journal of Contemporary Mathematics. Dec2025, Vol. 46 Issue 4, p367-382. 16p.\n\nPDF Full Text\n\n  2. 2\n\n[Input] [Input]\n\nAcademic Journal\n\n## An advanced resilient ambiguity resolution strategy accounting for non-Gaussian distribution for urban GNSS real-time kinematic positioning.\n\nAuthors: Zhan, Wei He, Xiufeng Huang, Yijie et al.\n\nSource: Advances in Space Research. Aug2026, Vol. 78 Issue 3, p2085-2099. 15p.\n\nSubjects: Distribution (Probability theory), Error analysis in mathematics, Gaussian distribution, Global Positioning System, Cities & towns, 